  "changes": [
    {
      "file": "src/city-broadphase.js",
      "change": "Preserve SAP candidate ordering and Cannon narrow phase. Skip static/static and sleeping/sleeping pair enumeration. Use AABB overlap rejection. Cache static collider bounds in 12-metre XZ cells and query only nearby cells plus moving/global bodies. Ground planes and large queries have bounded fallbacks. Add/remove invalidates the cache; static collider transforms must also mark broadphase dirty as usual."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/traffic.js",
      "change": "Civilian full physics enters within 24m and leaves beyond 36m. Predict closest relative approach 0.8 seconds ahead; check every 0.05 seconds. Nearby physical neighbors and contacts have bounded retention; remote contacts beyond 60m and remote maneuvers cannot retain physical bodies indefinitely. Far civilians continue logical route movement and traffic rules. Police physical-only behavior is retained."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/vehicle.js",
      "change": "Install CityBroadphase on the owned world. No change to 120Hz integration, solver iterations, vehicle forces, collision shapes, player tuning or damage rules."
    }
  ],
  "visuals": "No civilian mesh/geometry/material/model edits. Geometry identity and vertex contents are checked across physics-zone switches; civilians already disable damage. The number of traffic vehicles, lighting, DPR, shadows, blur and draw distance are unchanged.",
